r(".excalidraw-wysiwyg-preview")!.querySelectorAll("span")`. Popovers: the colour trigger renders aria-label={label} (Stroke/Background/Highlight) and data-openpopup={type}; open with a ResizeObserver stub then `fireEvent.click(document.querySelector('[aria-label="Highlight"]')!)` (same as togglePopover in ../tests/test-utils, which is not imported). Colours are stored as canonical lowercase hex. Cases, one `it` each, expected offsets computed from the strings, no it.skip/it.todo, no weakened assertions: A1 select 20..25 ('120ms'), run('changeStrokeColor','#e03131') -> text().textStyles toEqual [{start:20,end:25,color:'#e03131'}] and text().strokeColor unchanged from before; A2 same with run('changeTextHighlight','#ffec99') -> [{start:20,end:25,highlight:'#ffec99'}]; A3 editor.setSelectionRange(3,3) then run('changeStrokeColor','#e03131') -> strokeColor '#e03131' and textStyles undefined; A4 after A1, updateTextEditor(editor,'XBid request timeout 120ms') -> [{start:21,end:26,color:'#e03131'}], then updateTextEditor(editor,'XBid request timeout 12a0ms') -> [{start:21,end:27,color:'#e03131'}]; A5 after A1, Ctrl+Shift+> -> fontSize changed and textStyles still [{start:20,end:25,color:'#e03131'}]; A6 rectangle label 'Hello world', select 0..5, run stroke -> bound text textStyles [{start:0,end:5,color:'#e03131'}]; A7 sticky note: type 'Hello world', select 0..5, run stroke -> label textStyles [{start:0,end:5,color:'#e03131'}] and note.strokeColor unchanged; then open Highlight trigger -> h.state.openPopup === 'textHighlight' and the Background trigger's aria-expanded is not 'true'; A8 after A1 + exitTextEditor, Keyboard.undo() -> textStyles undefined, Keyboard.redo() -> [{start:20,end:25,color:'#e03131'}]; A9 after A1 and run('changeTextHighlight','#ffec99') on the same selection, exitTextEditor, re-enter edit -> a preview span with textContent '120ms' has non-empty style.color and style.backgroundColor.

